.wrangler/
node_modules/
*.log

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Extension zips are NOT committed. They used to be, so Pages could serve
# /chrome-store/*.zip, but the download was withdrawn: the extension's backend
# was never built (nothing serves /api/jobs or /api/sessions), so the published
# zip was a product that could only ever fail. With them tracked, `git add -A`
# quietly restored them the moment a deploy regenerated one on disk — which is
# exactly how they came back after being removed in 74c086b.
#
# Consequence to know before re-shipping: wrangler uploads what is present on
# disk, and deploy-local.sh only rebuilds these when SHIP_EXTENSION=1. If you
# implement the backend and opt in, you will likely also need to drop the
# `chrome-store/*.zip` line above so the regenerated zip is tracked again.
chrome-store/*.zip
version.txt
